  "mappingLimit": "Only unambiguous saved classifications map to named source industries. Broad manufacturing, telecommunications, insurance, building services and education classifications do not establish the narrower report industry; use the sourced overall median rather than a guessed industry match.",
  "approvedOverallFallback": "For an employer outside the named small-business industries, use the all-small-business median of 27 days as an explicit opening estimate under CTO approval 2026-10-02; no guessed industry multiplier. After opening, use the game's recorded comparable employer cash instead of this research bootstrap.",
  "estimationLimit": "JPMC observes average bank-account balances divided by ALL cash debits in a selected, metropolitan Chase sample, including employer and nonemployer businesses. Payroll plus IRS accounting nonwage costs is an unmeasured cash-debit proxy: accounting costs can include noncash depreciation and omit tax, capital expenditure, debt service, owner draws and other debits. Generated legal form, total firm size, banking coverage, 2021/local/territorial applicability and the source of the owner capital are unobserved. No owner contribution, appropriation, lending transaction, refill, future deficit or survival guarantee is established.",
  "dispersionLimit": "Observed 25th–75th percentiles are cohort dispersion, not a mean standard error, a universal minimum/maximum, an individual confidence interval, an actor assignment, a parameter-specific coefficient range or evidence for owner equity.",
  "openingCalendarRecipe": "Count each currently owned active recorded commitment only over opening date through December 31. Divide payroll plus compatible nonwage estimate over the same window by its actual calendar-day count. January 1 spans 365 or 366 days; a midyear opening does not invent pre-opening contracts. No future attendance or receipt is generated."
